From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:59:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] yblod-53: update YBLOD's system add-ons from its own
 repository only

yblod-20 let every optional system add-on take updates from any
installed third-party repository (m_latestPrivateVersions), bypassing
the origin pinning that protects system add-ons: any repository a user
installed could replace them.

The branch exists for the add-ons YBLOD pre-installs from
repository.dangerouslaser (Estuary YBLOD, the LG edition's webOS add-on
and the repository add-on itself). Look for their updates in that
repository's entries of m_latestVersionsByRepo only (keyed by the
repository's id, which is the origin of each remote add-on; disabled
repositories are not loaded). As for an add-on installed from a
third-party repository, which always updates from its origin repository,
the "update official add-ons from" mode is not consulted: it defaults to
official repositories only, so honouring it would stop these add-ons
from ever updating. The automatic-update setting and per-add-on update
rules still apply downstream (CRepositoryUpdater,
CAddonMgr::GetAddonUpdateCandidates).
---
 xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp b/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
index 2fd7668..43f838c 100644
--- a/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ namespace
 {
 constexpr auto ALL_ADDON_IDS = "";
 constexpr auto ALL_REPOSITORIES = nullptr;
+// The repository that updates the optional system add-ons YBLOD pre-installs.
+constexpr auto YBLOD_REPOSITORY = "repository.dangerouslaser";
 } // anonymous namespace
 
 using namespace ADDON;
@@ -262,13 +264,17 @@ bool CAddonRepos::DoAddonUpdateCheck(const std::shared_ptr<IAddon>& addon,
       }
     }
   }
-  // YBLOD: optional system add-ons pre-installed from a third-party repository (the LG edition's
-  // skin and webOS add-on) keep the system origin, so they would only ever be updated from the
-  // official repositories. Also take updates from an installed repository that carries them.
+  // YBLOD: the optional system add-ons YBLOD pre-installs from its own repository (Estuary
+  // YBLOD, the LG edition's webOS add-on and the repository itself) keep the system origin, so
+  // they would only ever be updated from the official repositories. Take their updates from that
+  // repository and no other: like an add-on installed from a third-party repository, which
+  // updates from its origin repository whatever the update mode.
   else if (addon->Origin() == ORIGIN_SYSTEM && !hasOfficialUpdate &&
            CServiceBroker::GetAddonMgr().IsOptionalSystemAddon(addon->ID()))
   {
-    FindAddonAndCheckForUpdate(addon, m_latestPrivateVersions, update);
+    const auto repoEntryIt = m_latestVersionsByRepo.find(YBLOD_REPOSITORY);
+    if (repoEntryIt != m_latestVersionsByRepo.end())
+      FindAddonAndCheckForUpdate(addon, repoEntryIt->second, update);
   }
 
   if (update)
